      "id": 252997,
      "name": "Trajector",
      "username": "Trajector",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
      "created_at": "2023-07-01T17:11:16.721Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Finally got a listen, and I think this story in particular is a great example of how much the impact and success of a story depends on the detailed writing that doesn’t happen on these episodes. Just about everything in this story depends on the 2/3 of the issue that is internal monologue for the main character. It could come off really well, with the character reflecting on their life story and grappling with the philosophy of their moral decisions (through the lens of their religion, to greater or lesser extent). Or the internal arguments could totally fall flat with readers. From the outline, we really don’t know! But I always like when a story really tries to address the moral questions involved, and it sure sounds like they created a plot framework where that attempt could happen.</p>",
      "post_number": 9,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2023-07-01T17:11:16.721Z",
