      "id": 264967,
      "name": "",
      "username": "LonelyMan",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/f4b2a3/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2026-01-29T14:17:20.383Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Make him a French monster and name him Honore de Baritone.</p>\n<p>“Do you know what an Italian is!?” <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/rofl.png?v=12\" title=\":rofl:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":rofl:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"><img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/rofl.png?v=12\" title=\":rofl:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":rofl:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"><img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/rofl.png?v=12\" title=\":rofl:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":rofl:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>This is one of the best stories they’ve ever told.  The sense of despair and futility pervading this guy’s persistent bad choices, and Fanatic’s implacable judginess, form a beautiful two sided coin of inevitability.</p>\n<p>“Have some taste! Don’t eat paste!”</p>\n<p>Biomancer is based on a real person; I guarantee that if both were given full modern socio historical and political and cultural gaming understanding of their Sentinel Comics personas, Zosimos Alchemista would be a lot angrier and sadder and more scandalized about BM than Robert Johnson would be about Rambler.</p>",
      "post_number": 10,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2026-01-29T15:21:14.562Z",
